}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le01ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "Imagine we are working on a very important project, and we are doing the requirement analysis, which is always the starting point of any project.<br/>\nRequirement analysis is a process which encircles several tasks required to define the needs and conditions for a new project or product; it encourages all the contradictory, and conflicting requirements of various stakeholders. Analysts always have to set the project by analyzing, documenting, validating and managing the requirements the system needs to be successful. Requirement analysis is crucial for the development of the project."}, {"time": "40000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Requirement analysis is usually a very complex procedure. Let's find out more details to understand it. <br>Requirement analysis is always a long process in which participants have to deal with thousands of requirements, examine and record data using several techniques, accessing to files and downloading relevant information. Requirements have to be documented, measurable, and traceable among other characteristics; the purpose of those tasks is to identify business needs and opportunities and to collect detailed information for system design. <br>As we are doing the requirement analysis of a project, we need to know step by step how it works. <br>"}, {"time": "84000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "There are three main tasks in requirement analysis; first, we have requirement gathering or elicitation, in this step, analysts talk to all the stakeholders and participants of the project to determine what the requirements are. The second step is to analyze requirements; in this step, analysts decide if there are some unclear, incomplete, or contradictory requirements and solve the problems. The last step is to record the requirements using different tools, such as documents or user stories. Analysts keep track of all the requirements for the development of the project.      <br>The project we are working on is very complex, but we have to be analytic, and assertive to make the project work."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le01ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}